  "review_conclusions": [
    "ConfigStore clone shares an immutable-JSON owner map. JSON comparison/typed serde/deep copies and replaced-owner destruction stay outside the map lock; owner identity is rechecked before changed-value publication. Persistence snapshots retain only the ConfigStore, not the Core.",
    "Cleanup context snapshots registered index/generation/name only after stopping, closed admission and drained calls/initializers. Every borrow rechecks identity and state; clones the optional instance under the registry lock; downcast and callback occur after unlock. No instance returns false; an owning Arc is not an ordinary admission permit.",
    "Module/PluginContext keep CoreWeak and optional source-derived paths. Core plugin factories use full registered service identity and initially None roots. VM path derivation does not create directories or equate package-root presence with source-root presence.",
    "Descriptors are passive owned declarations with shared factory/dependency owners. Constructors/builders neither register nor invoke factories. Registration validates module/kind and reserves slot identities; complete graph freezing separately validates missing/duplicate/direct cross-owner edges and cycles and caches only successful construction.",
    "Module root order uses InitLevel plus input order and authored dependency order; service traversal uses lexical edge views while validation retains authored first-invalid precedence. Explicit DFS frames bound native call stack usage; shutdown reverses all service names including Lazy services. Frozen topology does not prove live instance or admission state.",
    "RegistryName owns the exact canonical string; equality/hash/Borrow/serde share that authority. The final two ASCII dots delimit namespaced modules; validated cached offsets stay on UTF-8 boundaries. Manual deserialization reuses new(); no trim, case conversion or registry existence claim is introduced.",
    "Factories run after dependency resolution outside registry locks; returned errors/panics map through existing typed errors and successful values still require slot/generation/phase checks before publication. Type-erased static Arc ownership and Runtime lifecycle admission remain distinct.",
    "All five owned fixture files and their actual assertions were read. Ignored timing fixtures describe their own measured operation and threshold only; neither performance results nor Rust/Cargo execution are claimed. 91 source-text operands remain identical, including four existing absent anchors tracked by CR-RUNTIME-TESTS-STRUCT-0019."
  ],
